First Author: Kampaktsis
Title: State-of-the-art machine learning algorithms for the prediction of outcomes after contemporary heart transplantation: Results from the UNOS database
Source number: 24  ￼

Very short summary: This retrospective UNOS study developed and internally validated machine-learning models for outcome prediction after contemporary heart transplantation using only pre-transplant variables. Five key findings were: (1) the cohort included 18,625 adult isolated heart transplant recipients from 2010–2018; (2) 1-year mortality was 12.5% with 2,334 deaths; (3) 39 of 134 pre-transplant variables were selected for the main 1-year model; (4) Adaboost had the best discrimination for 1-year survival with AUC 0.689, outperforming IMPACT score AUC 0.569; and (5) secondary models for 3-year survival, 5-year survival, and acute rejection achieved AUCs of 0.629, 0.609, and 0.610, respectively. Figures 1–2 and Tables 1–2 were directly used for this extraction.  ￼

